{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-22410","model_call":4,"request":{"op":"document","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1586499613#9_2944666724"},"record":{"query":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1586499613#9_2944666724","op":"document"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_48_1586499613#9_2944666724","document":"Accredited Online Degrees & Programs | OnlineDegrees.com ... Best Online Degrees for 2020 Best Online Degrees for 2020 From the experts who also bring you: Is An Online Degree Program Right for You? Top Reasons to Choose An Online Degree Program Frequently Asked Questions How does an online degree program work? Are online college degrees legitimate? Is an online college degree worth it? Are online degrees respected by employers? What is the earning potential by degree level? What online degrees are available? How to apply for a degree online? Is financial aid available for online degrees? Types of Online Degrees Featured Online Degree Programs How to Select the Best Online Degree Program and School Degree & Career Match-Up Tool Find Online Degree Programs in Your State SELECT A STATE Before You Enroll Consider financial aid options and entry-level tests Featured Articles 15 Best Online Business Degrees 2020 15 Best Online Healthcare Degrees 2020 10 Successful Online Learning Strategies 15 Best Small Cities For New Grads 2019 15 Best Midsize Cities For New Grads 2019 What Can You Do With A Degree In Humanities?  ... Are online degrees respected by employers? According to a study on online degrees, employers are more likely to consider the reputation of the institution from which the degree was earned as opposed to the medium of education. Online college degrees are no different from those earned in a traditional campus-based environment. In fact, many online college degree programs undergo the same stringent tests as traditional degree programs to gain accreditation. Additionally, employers who have taken online courses are more likely to prefer candidates with online degrees due to the perception that online degree programs can build soft skills in students. The study concludes by stating that as more and more employers have online degrees themselves, the acceptance of online education is rising. What is the earning potential by degree level? The table below lists the earning potential by degree levels using 2019 data from the BLS: Degree Held Median Weekly Earnings High school diploma, no college $746 Some college, no degree $833 Associate degree $887 Bachelor's degree $1,248 Master's degree $1,497 Professional degree $1,861 Doctoral degree $1,883 Earning potential can vary by the field you work in as well as your position in a company. More advanced  degrees can lead to jobs with more responsibility as well as higher wages.","ok":true,"op":"document"},"time":21},"model_calls":4,"document_judgments":3,"relevance_3":2,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
