{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-22410","model_call":29,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ employers (+ accept accepted respect respected) \"online degree\" accreditation reputation)"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ employers (+ accept accepted respect respected) \"online degree\" accreditation reputation)"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_88438645#5_143602035","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2712","rank":1,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_88438645#5_143602035\" , \"end_char\": 4105.000000 , \"headings\": \"Are Online Degrees as Respected as Traditional Degrees? Are Online Degrees as Respected as Traditional Degrees? Do <cover>Employers Respect Online Degrees? Tips for Finding a Respected Online Degree 2. Accreditation 3. How quickly can you earn the degree? 4. Quality of the school’s graduates Further Reading FAQ What is the Most Respected Online University? \" , \"segment\": \"Tips for Finding a Respected Online Degree If you’re looking to go back to school online, consider these six things to evaluate a quality online degree program. Reputation</cover>Does the school you’re considering have a brick-and-mortar location or is it online only? Schools that have physical campuses are viewed as more credible. If the school only has a P.O. box or suite number, employers will view it as a red flag. 2. Accreditation The Department of Education says that accreditation is essential to credibility. Make sure that the school you plan to attend is recognized by the Council for Higher Education Accreditation. "},"time":162},"model_calls":29,"document_judgments":26,"relevance_3":19,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
