{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-22410","model_call":40,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2716"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q2716"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_271224719#10_521625050","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2716","rank":4,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_271224719#10_521625050\" , \"end_char\": 6299.000000 , \"headings\": \"How Credible Are Online Degrees? How Credible Are Online Degrees? Online Degrees Gaining Acceptance Factors That Make <cover>Online Degrees Credible University Reputation Accreditation Time to Earn Curriculum Rigor Summary Additional Resources References \" , \"segment\": \"There are still some more traditional employers who may not accept </cover>online degree credentials, however. These are people who are resistant to change and traditional in terms of education and qualifications. But they are increasingly in the minority in recent years, the evidence suggests. Factors That Make Online Degrees Credible There is little doubt that online degrees are generally more accepted today than they were a decade ago. But not every online degree is created the same. If you are looking at an online bachelor’s or master’s program, employers report that there are several very important factors that make online degrees increase in credibility. There are still ‘diploma mills’ out there that churn out largely worthless degrees that are ‘accredited’ by unknown bodies of little value. You can ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_271224719#10_521625050","rank":4,"relevance":3}]},"time":15},"model_calls":40,"document_judgments":36,"relevance_3":24,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
