{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-22410","model_call":40,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2716"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q2716"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_329956433#5_706740846","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2716","rank":5,"snippet":"Full-Time Equivalent Student 2019-2020 Grants Federal Loans Applying for Aid How Much Do Bachelor's Degree-Holders Make? How Do I Choose an Online Bachelor's Degree? What Are the Types of Bachelor's Degrees? What Are the Most Popular Majors? Applying to an Online Bachelor's Program Common Admission Requirements ACT or SAT Scores GED Scores Recommendation Letters High School Transcripts GPA Minimum Essay/Personal Statement Interview With an Expert Lynne Lander Fleisher Related Pages \" , \"segment\": \"Additionally, U.S. News & World Report notes that most <cover>employers now accept online degrees. Earning an online degree from an accredited </cover>institution is key for success, as is selecting a school with strong brand recognition in the student's major field of study. Since many colleges and universities use the same curricula for online and in-person degrees, the perception of online degrees among employers should continue to improve. Annual Trends in Online Education The Benefits and Challenges of Online Learning Online vs. Campus-Based Bachelor's Degrees Expand All Full-Time, On-Campus Classes Benefits Unrestricted access to libraries, computer labs, and other campus resources Courses with labs, practicum training, and other practical components","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_271224719#10_521625050","rank":4,"relevance":3}]},"time":9},"model_calls":40,"document_judgments":36,"relevance_3":24,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
