{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-22410","model_call":50,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"online degree\" \"taken seriously\" employers accreditation)"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"online degree\" \"taken seriously\" employers accreditation)"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_36_1027815171#5_2059470165","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q2723","rank":1,"snippet":"a program that is right for you. \" , \"segment\": \"Enter the online bachelor’s in engineering, designed for those who cannot attend a traditional college because of financial or other constraints. The days when an online degree meant dubious respectability are well in the past, and an <cover>online degree can provide a path to a high quality, affordable education that will be taken seriously by employers. But there are a lot of options out there for online engineering degrees and finding the right program at the right price can be rather mind-numbingly tedious. So we at College Choice have done the leg-work for you. Our ranking features 20 of the cheapest online engineering programs available. These cover a broad range of engineering specializations—from Mechanical to Software Engineering. And because it is difficult to over-emphasize the importance of proper accreditation, </cover>we have made sure that all the schools on this list have regional accreditation, and many programs have further accreditation from some of the main STEM Accreditation bodies: ABET (Accreditation Board for Engineering and Technology) ATMAE (Association of Technology, Management and Applied Engineering) IFSAC (International Fire Service Accreditation Congress) It is important "},"time":60},"model_calls":50,"document_judgments":45,"relevance_3":29,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
