{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-22410","model_call":53,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q2725"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q2725"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_321106515#2_695220629","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2725","rank":2,"snippet":"an Online Degree Worth It? Are Online Degrees Easier Than On-Campus Programs? Plan Ahead Expect the Unexpected Build Your Skills Are Online Degrees More Affordable Than Studying On Campus? Explore Employer Partnerships Consider Transfer Credit Understand College Costs and Fees<cover>Are Online Degrees Respected or Taken Seriously? Can Online Degrees Get You a Job? Return on Investment Willingness to Recommend Perception of Quality \" , \"segment\": \"While, personally, I have never liked the term \\\"online degree,\\\" it is commonly used to describe a college degree that is earned through online courses and programs rather than by attending on-campus classes. The tendency to always qualify an education as \\\"online,\\\" however, may contribute to myths about the online format compared to a traditional, on-campus education. These myths often relate to how difficult the degrees are to complete, how they compare in terms of costs, and how they are received or respected by employers </cover>after graduation. What can you expect as an online student? Will the experience be worth your time, effort, and resources? Below are my answers to a few of the most frequently asked questions. Are Online Degrees Easier Than On-Campus Programs? Probably "},"time":10},"model_calls":53,"document_judgments":48,"relevance_3":30,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
